==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=refuge}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|en|bʰewg}}
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|refuge}}, from {{der|en|la|refugium}}, from {{m|la|re-}} + {{m|la|fugiō||flee}}. {{doublet|lang=en|refugium}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-refuge.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{IPA|/ˈɹɛfjuːdʒ/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A state of [[safety]], [[protection]] or [[shelter]].
#* {{rfdate||and other bibliographic particulars, eg, title of work, page, url}} {{w|John Milton}}
#*: Rocks, dens, and caves! But I in none of these / Find place or '''refuge'''.
# A [[place]] providing safety, protection or shelter.
#* {{quote-book|year=1898|author={{w|Winston Churchill (novelist)|Winston Churchill}}| title={{w|The Celebrity}}| chapter=4| passage=One morning I had been driven to the precarious '''refuge''' afforded by the steps of the inn, after rejecting offers from the Celebrity to join him in a variety of amusements. But even here I was not free from interruption, for he was seated on a horse-block below me, playing with a fox terrier.}}
# Something or someone turned to for safety or [[assistance]]; a [[recourse]] or [[resort]].
#* {{quote-journal|date=December 21, 2011|author=Helen Pidd|work=the Guardian
|title=[http://www.guardian.co.uk/world/2011/dec/21/europe-migrants-crisis-irish-portuguese Europeans migrate south as continent drifts deeper into crisis]
|passage=Since its conception, the European Union has been a haven for those seeking '''refuge''' from war, persecution and poverty in other parts of the world.}}
# An [[expedient]] to secure protection or defence.
#* {{rfdate||and other bibliographic particulars, eg, title of work, page, url, act, scene, line}} {{w|William Shakespeare}}
#*: Their latest '''refuge''' / Was to send him.
#* {{quote-book|year=a. 1639|author={{w|Henry Wotton}}| title=An Essay on the Education of Children, in the First Rudiments of Learning| location=London| publisher=T. Waller| year_published=1753| page=17| pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=G6BbAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA17| passage=This is occaſioned by this, that too too<!-- reduplication present in original --> often the Teaching of a Grammar School is the ordinary '''Refuge''' that deſperate Perſons as to any other Employment in good Learning betake themſelves to; whilﬅ but a few know themſelves ſuited with intellectual and moral Abilities, and fewer have that Encouragement, when they undertake it, their Pains deſerve.}}
# A [[refuge island]].

